<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Internet Protocol Guide</title>
    <style>
        body {
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            background: #eafaff;
            padding: 25px;
        }
        .container {
            max-width: 850px;
            margin: auto;
            background: white;
            padding: 25px;
            border-radius: 16px;
        }
        h1 { text-align: center; color: #087a9e; }
        .protocol {
            background: #e4f7fc;
            padding: 18px;
            margin: 15px 0;
            border-radius: 12px;
        }
        h2 { color: #087a9e; }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="container">
    <h1>🌐 Internet Protocol Guide</h1>

    <div class="protocol">
        <h2>HTTP</h2>
        <p>Transfers information between web browsers and web servers.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="protocol">
        <h2>HTTPS</h2>
        <p>Uses encryption to help protect data exchanged with a website.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="protocol">
        <h2>TCP/IP</h2>
        <p>A suite of networking protocols that enables devices to communicate across networks.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="protocol">
        <h2>DNS</h2>
        <p>Helps translate domain names into IP addresses.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="protocol">
        <h2>FTP</h2>
        <p>A protocol designed for transferring files between systems.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="protocol">
        <h2>Why Protocols Matter</h2>
        <p>Protocols define common rules that allow different devices and applications to communicate.</p>
    </div>
</div>
</body>
</html>
